data: {"id":"chatcmpl-20261013154556759967739c955d568uclIdWGJ","created":1791906357,"object":"chat.completion.chunk","model":"glm-5.3-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_65d7547d161c4da5ae4b94cc","index":0,"type":"function","function":{"name":"write","arguments":"{\"content\":\"BOUNDS AND COVERAGE OF THE VERIFICATION\\n=======================================\\n\\nClaim verified:  For all integers x, (x + 1) * (x - 1) = x^2 - 1.\\nSpecification:   forall x : Int. (x + 1) * (x - 1) = x^2 - 1   (spec.txt)\\n\\n1. DOMAIN OF THE CLAIM\\n----------------------\\nThe domain is ALL integers Z = {..., -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, ...}: an infinite,\\nunbounded, two-sided domain. The claim is universally quantified over\\nthis entire set; there is no subrange restriction in the statement.\\n\\n2. PROOF METHOD AND ITS COVERAGE\\n--------------------------------\\nMethod: symbolic equational proof over the integers, viewed as a\\ncommutative ring (proof.txt). 14 rewrite steps citing only the four\\npermitted axioms (A1-A4) plus disclosed notational conventions (C1-C6)\\nand two internally derived lemmas (L1, L2), closed by universal\\ngeneralization over an arbitrary x.\\n\\nCoverage: EXHAUSTIVE over the stated domain. The generalization step\\ncovers every integer simultaneously — including values outside any\\nfinite test range, arbitrarily large magnitudes, and negative values —\\nbecause the derivation never uses a particular value of x. Validity in\\nfact extends beyond Z: the argument holds in every commutative ring\\n(e.g., rationals, reals, polynomials), since no integer-specific axioms\\n(induction, ordering, etc.) were used.\\n\\n3. EMPIRICAL CHECK AND ITS LIMITATIONS\\n--------------------------------------\\nMethod: finite enumeration of x in [-100, 100] (201 values) with exact\\nbignum arithmetic (counterexample_check.txt).\\n\\nLimitations of the empirical check:\\n  - NON-EXHAUSTIVE: it covers 201 of infinitely many integers. Passing\\n    on a finite prefix can never establish the universally quantified\\n    claim, even if extended to millions of values.\\n  - Bounds: x in [-100, 100] only; nothing is tested for |x| > 100.\\n  - It can only REFUTE, never CONFIRM: its sound role is as a\\n    falsification screen, and it found no counterexample.\\n  - Correctness of the check itself rests on the shell/Python\\n    arithmetic semantics, not on the proof.\\n\\n4. LIMITATIONS OF THE PROOF CERTIFICATE / CHECKER\\n-------------------------------------------------\\n  - The certificate is a human-readable text derivation, not machine\\n    checked by an independent theorem prover; its correctness rests on\\n    the audit trail of citations (audit.txt) and on manual review.\\n  - Conventions C1-C4 (identities/annihilation for 0 and 1) are declared\\n    as the meaning of the constants rather than derived from the four\\n    permitted axioms; audit.txt records this as the minimal semantic\\n    scaffolding needed to interpret the claim. A stricter standard\\n    would require deriving them or admitting ring axioms explicitly.\\n  - Associativity (C5) is treated as notational regrouping of flat\\n    n-ary expressions rather than an explicitly cited axiom.\\n  - Equality is used with its standard logical properties\\n    (reflexivity, symmetry, transitivity, substitutivity) as ambient\\n    rules of equational reasoning; these are logic, not assumptions\\n    about integers, but they are not formally listed in proof.txt.\\n  - The checker scripts validate syntax and cited justifications;\\n    they do not independently re-derive the algebra from first\\n    principles.\\n\\n5. OVERALL VERDICT\\n------------------\\n  Proof (symbolic): covers the full domain Z — COMPLETE.\\n  Testing (finite): covers 201 of infinitely many values — SOUND AS A\\n                    FALSIFICATION SCREEN ONLY; it adds no positive\\n                    coverage beyond sanity checking.\\n  Residual assurance rests on the proof, not on the